{
  "abstract": "For positive integers k and p, among finite simple connected graphs with distance-k packing number p, the maximum sum of the six pairwise shortest distances on four distinct vertices is 6k + 4(k+1)(p−1). A distance-k packing requires all its pairwise distances to exceed k. More generally, for nonnegative integer terminal weights the maximum product-weighted sum is k times the total weight of the six pairs plus (k+1)(p−1) times the maximum weighted cut on the four terminals. Both endpoints prove the universal bound and construct an attaining connected graph with exact packing number p.",
